---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Credentials from '../components/Credentials.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import portrait from '../assets/photos/lyncia-portrait.jpg';
import presenting from '../assets/photos/lyncia-presenting.jpg';

const person = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: site.owner,
  jobTitle: 'Coach and facilitator',
  worksFor: { '@id': `${site.url}/#business` },
  url: `${site.url}/about`,
  sameAs: [site.social.linkedin],
  knowsAbout: ['Coaching', 'Gallup CliftonStrengths', 'Communication skills', 'Leadership development', 'NLP'],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Lyncia Podmore, Coach & Facilitator, Wellington"
  description="Lyncia Podmore is a Wellington-based coach, Gallup Certified Strengths Coach and accredited Transforming Communication trainer. Calm, grounded coaching with no hype."
  schema={[person]}
>
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-b from-mint-soft to-cream">
    <div class="container-page grid items-center gap-12 py-14 sm:py-20 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.2fr]">
      <Image src={portrait} alt="Lyncia Podmore" widths={[400, 700]} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 460px, 90vw" class="mx-auto aspect-[4/5] w-full max-w-md rounded-[2rem] object-cover shadow-xl" loading="eager" />
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-medium sm:text-5xl">Hi, I'm Lyncia</h1>
        <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-lg text-muted">
          <p>
            I decided to become a coach after "career coaching" myself in 2007. It proved to be the right decision. I love
            what I do. Every day, and every conversation, brings something different.
          </p>
          <p>
            I'm based in Wellington, with an office in the central city. Technology means I work with people all over New
            Zealand and further afield too.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 sm:py-20">
    <div class="container-page max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl">What I believe</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-lg text-muted">
        <p>
          I'm not interested in the rah-rah side of coaching: the "be the best, lead your extraordinary life" stuff. I
          think a lot of the self-help industry is quite selfish, and it isn't always good for us. It can make us more
          inward-looking, not less.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most of us won't lead extraordinary lives. But nearly everyone can lead a happy and fulfilling one, where you get
          to do things you enjoy, you have good relationships, and you're using what you're good at. We're not islands. Our
          lives are tied up with the people around us, and a good life is one that the people we care about are happy to
          be part of too.
        </p>
        <p>
          And I genuinely believe there's nothing wrong with most of us. Things just don't go right sometimes. If we can
          find out why, there's usually something we can do about it. You can learn to communicate better, to listen
          better, to present yourself well. What you can't do is become someone else, and you don't need to.
        </p>
        <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-teal pl-5 font-display text-xl text-navy">
          "Learn to want what you already have." Let's look at what you've already got, and build on that.
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-mint-soft py-16 sm:py-20">
    <div class="container-page grid items-center gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl">Sounding board, thinking partner, listening post</h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg text-muted">
          For some people I'm a coach working towards a specific goal. For others, especially leaders, I'm a trusted
          listening post: someone to talk things over with, who will ask "How do you think that will land with Mary?" or
          "What do you know about her that makes that a good idea?"
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-muted">
          Underneath everything I do are three things: <strong class="text-navy">strengths</strong>,
          <strong class="text-navy">communication</strong>, and the <strong class="text-navy">confidence</strong> that
          grows when you understand both.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Image src={presenting} alt="Lyncia presenting at a workshop" widths={[500, 800]} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 540px, 90vw" class="aspect-[4/3] w-full rounded-3xl object-cover" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 sm:py-20">
    <div class="container-page max-w-4xl">
      <Credentials />
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTA />
</BaseLayout>
